      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2f057cabac035d05a6e146|full_name}: Please do not lump people with legitimate concerns together with those that want to break ToS.\nAs far as kernel-level being harder to bypass. It does seem that the Proton version of EAC is not kernel level.\nI have not verified it myself yet, but I know people have been able to run it inside LXC containers at the very least. Which doesn't mean it can't be kernel level, but that it is unlikely as containers tend to limit what nodes get passed in /dev for instance and other ways that something could interact with certain kernel drivers.\nBesides if it is malicious modders you are worried about, they seem to have already bypassed EAC. The information on how to do so is out there, too... It's not really accessible to the skids just yet though.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
