        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I mean honestly EAC was never necessary, this is a social platform and a grand majority of all issues presented by exploiters could have all been resolved by improving server-side security. I think it's overkill for a game like this and was a band-aid solution so developers wouldn't have to invest more into securing and improving their game, but it's not like they would change it or rollback at this point. My main gripe with EAC is the additional performance tax on top of an already demanding game, which isn't even competitive at all in nature and relies on performance for a smooth experience. Not to mention the complications it can cause on varying systems.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
